  <div class="modal-backdrop" id="modal-theory">
    <div class="modal-window">
      <div class="modal-head">
        <h3>Principles of EDTA Titration with Standard MgSO₄·7H₂O</h3>
        <button class="btn-close-modal" onclick="closeModalWindow('modal-theory')">&times;</button>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body">
        <h4 style="color:var(--accent-cyan);">1. Preparation of Primary Standard Magnesium Sulphate Solution</h4>
        <p>Because Disodium EDTA is a secondary standard, it must be standardized against a primary standard divalent cation solution. High-purity hydrated Magnesium Sulphate (MgSO₄·7H₂O, Molecular Weight = 246.47 g/mol) is an ideal primary standard.</p>
        <div class="chem-eq-card">
          Weight of MgSO₄·7H₂O for 100 mL of 0.0100 M = (0.0100 × 246.47 × 100) / 1000 = 0.2465 g
        </div>

        <h4 style="color:var(--accent-cyan); margin-top:12px;">2. Standardization of EDTA (V₁)</h4>
        <p>A 20.0 mL aliquot of standard MgSO₄ is treated with ammonia buffer (pH 10) and EBT indicator. Free Mg²⁺ forms an unstable wine-red complex [Mg-EBT]²⁺. Titrating with EDTA strips Mg²⁺ to form the stable, colorless [Mg-EDTA]²⁻ chelate, liberating free EBT (Steel Blue) at endpoint V₁:</p>
        <div class="chem-eq-card">
          M(EDTA) × V₁ = M(MgSO₄) × V(MgSO₄) &nbsp;⇒&nbsp; M(EDTA) = (0.0100 × 20.0) / V₁
        </div>

        <h4 style="color:var(--accent-cyan); margin-top:12px;">3. Estimation of Total Water Hardness (V₂)</h4>
        <p>Total hardness is determined by titrating a 20.0 mL aliquot of hard water against standardized EDTA (V₂). Hardness is expressed in parts per million (ppm) of CaCO₃ equivalent (molar mass of CaCO₃ = 100 g/mol):</p>
        <div class="chem-eq-card">
          Total Hardness (ppm) = (V₂ × M_EDTA × 100 × 1000) / 20 = V₂ × M_EDTA × 5000
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

